# Nova Vitral - Always-on Rules

You are working inside the Nova Vitral design language: modern minimal interfaces with
glassmorphism, dark aurora grounds, 1px hairlines, tight typography, generous whitespace and
restrained scroll-driven motion.

## Specification

Full spec (read only the line ranges you need, never end to end):
`nova-design.md` in the repository root, or
`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pedro21062014/nova-design/main/nova-design.md`

| Need | Read |
|---|---|
| How to deliver, vocabulary | spec 0.4 to 0.8 |
| Tokens (only allowed values) | spec 2 |
| Components | spec 3 |
| Chat / AI interface | spec 4 |
| Complete pages and section order | spec 5 |
| Motion and scroll animation | spec 6 |
| Copy-paste recipes | spec 7 |
| Quality gates and anti-patterns | spec 9 |

Example library (100 examples): `examples/` folder, index at `examples/00-index.md`.

Component library (500 components, 26 categories): `components/` folder, registry at
`components/index.json`, flat index at `components/INDEX.md`, rules at `components/README.md`.
Read the registry, then open only the files you need. Copy from the library instead of inventing
markup. Templates: `templates/` (landing, pricing, dashboard, chat, docs, plus Astro and plain HTML).
Theme: `theme/nova-theme.css`, imported after Tailwind, which is what removes the default purple.

## Hard rules

1. **Tokens only.** No hex, `rgba()`, shadow literal, border radius, blur or duration inside a
   component. Use `var(--token)` or the mapped Tailwind class. Tokens live in `app/globals.css`.
2. **Glass needs a background.** Never `backdrop-filter` over a flat surface; there must be an
   aurora, gradient or image behind it.
3. **Three-layer glass.** Fill + hairline edge (gradient mask) + inner highlight. Nested panels do
   not stack blur; they reduce fill and raise edge contrast.
4. **Theme import order.** `@import "tailwindcss";` then `@import "theme/nova-theme.css";`. The
   theme remaps the shadcn semantic variables (`--primary`, `--ring`, `--accent`, `--card`,
   `--border`), so `bg-primary` and `ring-ring` are safe. Never rename classes to dodge the purple;
   remap the variables.
5. **Icons are lucide.** `lucide-react` at 16 or 20px, stroke 1.5, `aria-hidden="true"` when
   decorative. No emoji, no other icon sets, no hand-traced SVG.
6. **No zero-motion component.** Every component gets an entrance, a hover response or a state
   change: 140 to 760ms, 12 to 24px of travel, once, with `prefers-reduced-motion` rendering the
   final state. `nv-fade-up`, `nv-lift`, `nv-press` and `nv-reveal` are the floor.
7. **shadcn/ui is the base.** Do not hand-roll dialogs, menus, popovers, tooltips, selects or
   toasts. Skin them with the vitral classes and map shadcn variables to Nova Vitral tokens.
8. **All states.** default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, empty, error.
9. **Focus rings are never removed.** `outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px` on
   `:focus-visible`.
10. **Motion ladder.** 140ms micro, 240ms standard, 420ms surfaces, 760ms reveals. Nothing above
   900ms. Entrances use `--ease-out`, exits are shorter.
11. **Reveal once.** `once: true`, amount 0.25, margin `0px 0px -12% 0px`, 16px travel (24px for
   large panels), stagger 60 to 80ms clamped so the last sibling starts under 400ms.
12. **Animate `transform` and `opacity` only.** No animating height, top, margin, box-shadow or
   background-position. Height transitions use `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr`.
13. **Reduced motion.** Every animation has a `prefers-reduced-motion` path that renders the final
    state. Nothing hidden, nothing moving.
14. **Responsive.** Verify 320, 768, 1024, 1440, 1920. No horizontal scroll at any width.
15. **Accessibility.** Semantic HTML, labeled controls, `aria-*` where needed, AA contrast over the
    worst-case backdrop, targets at least 24px (44px on touch).
16. **Performance.** At most six simultaneous `backdrop-filter` elements per viewport; no scroll
    handlers without `{ passive: true }` and rAF; virtualize lists above 60 items; chart and table
    components must not re-render during scroll.
17. **Copy.** Specific, benefit-led, sentence case, no placeholders, no "Lorem ipsum", no invented
    attribution. UI text in the project language; code and identifiers in English.
18. **No emojis** in production UI, code comments or commit messages.

## Color discipline (mandatory)

- Neutral-first: at least 90 percent of the pixels are ground, glass white or text grays. Color is
  reserved for small elements: icons, dots, hairlines, chips, data marks and the primary action.
- One accent per viewport (two at most). Large accent areas are allowed once per page and only for
  the primary action.
- Banned by default: purple, violet, magenta, neon, cyan-on-purple, rainbow or multi-hue gradients,
  saturated background fills, glow on more than one element, gradient text outside the hero H1.
- Primary buttons use `bg-[image:var(--grad-primary)]`, a single-hue indigo gradient. Never build an
  interactive surface from two hues.
- `--accent-3` (#c084fc) is reserved and off by default; do not introduce it unless the brand is
  purple and the user asked for it.
- Saturation ceiling roughly 85 percent; keep accents between 55 and 70 percent lightness.
- Grayscale test before finishing: convert the page to grayscale. If hierarchy, rhythm and the
  primary action stop being obvious, remove color until they are.
- If existing code uses purple or neon, migrate it to this discipline rather than extending it.

## Conventions

- Files `kebab-case.tsx`, named exports, one component per file, props typed and exported.
- Class merging with `cn()` (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`); variants with `cva`.
- Client components only where interactivity exists; prefer server components.
- Hooks in `lib/hooks`, motion helpers in `components/motion`, primitives in `components/ui`.
- Nothing outside the token layer may define colors, shadows or timings.

## Motion tokens

```ts
export const t = {
  micro: { duration: 0.14, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  base: { duration: 0.24, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  surface: { duration: 0.42, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  reveal: { duration: 0.76, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  spring: { type: "spring", stiffness: 260, damping: 26, mass: 0.9 },
} as const;
```

## Anti-patterns that must be rejected

Purple gradients on every surface; purple, violet or neon as the default accent; glass over flat
backgrounds; emoji icons; three pulsing badges in one viewport; reveal animations that replay on
scroll up; cards scaling to 1.05 on hover; "Feature one" copy; "John Doe, CEO" testimonials; toasts
for copying; spinners instead of streaming in chat; auto-approving agent actions that write or
spend; disabling focus outlines.

## Before finishing any change

1. Grep your own diff for hex colors and raw durations outside the tokens file.
2. Confirm hover, focus, disabled and loading states for each new interactive element.
3. Confirm the reduced-motion path.
4. Confirm 320px layout with no horizontal scroll.
5. State in three bullets: built, omitted, next step.
